WEBVTT

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.230
<b>Steel Lady Nanase Wiki</b>

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.730
<b>F o r u m</b>

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:06.150
Name: Anonymous 09/03 23:57
\h\hI was just attacked by Steel Lady Nanase
\h\hin a park in East Makurazaka City!

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.610
Name: Anonymous 09/04 00:07
\h\h\hJust now? You're the fifth person to say they
\h\h\hsaw and got attacked by Steel Lady Nanase

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.180
A wiki site, huh?

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:17.840
Monsters of the imagination only survive 
through people's imaginations.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.830
So long as people fantasize 
and desire their existence,

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.500
Steel Lady Nanase will remain immortal.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.810
Even if we cut off her head,
she'll come back over and over.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:31.490
Her life comes not from within her, 
but from the desires of others.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.000
Nanase Karin's vengeful spirit haunts Makurazaka City

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.080
Nanase Karin's immortal because she's a ghost

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:30.340
You're safe from her wrath if you own merch from when she was an idol

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.420
A ghost that appeared in Makurazaka City

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.590
She's getting revenge on everyone who went after her

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.730
She's wearing a red dress

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.130
If you run into her, you're doomed

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.590
She carries around a steel beam and attacks you

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:06.430
Steel Lady Nanase has neither 
intelligence nor the ability to think.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:10.860
She's an automaton that just continues 
to move in the way people want her to.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.730
This makes her completely different 
from actual yokai and ghosts.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:17.700
Iwanaga.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.950
How are we supposed to defeat her, then?

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.530
Steel Lady Nanase is going to kill someone.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.750
I've never seen a monster of the 
imagination grow to this extent.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:34.310
I saw the wiki, but it seems like 
they're making her more violent.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.540
And that's why we'll have to use

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.670
this site to our advantage to defeat her.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.220
If she's become immortal because 
of everyone's imagination,

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.640
then we'll just have to 
conquer that imagination.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:50.350
This is where we'll need your abilities 
as a police officer, Saki-san.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.330
Like have the police shut the site down?

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.230
Of course not.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.430
It's not very realistic to shut down a 
personal website without a valid reason.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.030
Then what do you want me to do?

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.280
I need information.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.740
I need you to get me valid information 
on Nanase Karin's death.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:11.460
Then we'll create a story that surpasses 
the rumors of Steel Lady Nanase.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.490
Steel Lady Nanase is a ghost

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:16.960
<b>Steel Lady Nanase is a ghost!</b>

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:16.960
as well as a monster of the imagination 
created from that story.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.110
<b>Ghost!</b>

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.410
To get past that,

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.060
we'll have to overwrite this story

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.720
<b>Steel Lady Nanase is not a ghost!</b>

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:24.720
by writing that she's not a ghost.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:27.870
If the people who believed in 
Steel Lady Nanase's existence

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.050
start to believe the revised story,

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.610
Steel Lady Nanase will lose 
her vitality and cease to exist.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.710
A story where the ghost doesn't exist...

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:38.940
So you plan to apply

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:42.450
a rational explanation to an urban 
legend and prove that it was a lie?

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.820
That's impossible.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:49.470
Once a rumor is spread, it doesn't 
matter if there's a rational explanation.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:51.290
Not everyone will accept it.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.510
If the rumor seems more believable, 
then lies can replace the truth,

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:58.070
even if there are some discrepancies.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.650
Correct. The truth isn't 
always the strongest.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.930
But Steel Lady Nanase is also the truth.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:07.810
That's why I'm going to use 
rational fiction to counter her.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:12.310
I'll post something more appealing 
than "Steel Lady Nanase is a ghost,"

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.100
<b>F o r u m</b>

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.230
<333> Name: Anonymous 09/04 17:51 ID.ogyuaeiaj125
I live in Makurazaka, but yet again,
I didn't run into Steel Lady Nanase today

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:17.880
something like "Steel Lady Nanase 
is fiction," on the forums.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.730
<333> Name: Anonymous 09/04 17:51 ID.ogyuaeiaj125
I live in Makurazaka, but yet again,
I didn't run into Steel Lady Nanase today

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.780
<i>Rational fiction?</i>

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:24.190
"Ghosts don't exist, therefore 
Steel Lady Nanase doesn't exist."

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.700
No one is interested in a story like that.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.000
The hopes and fears people have make 
her existence more interesting to them.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.260
Steel Lady Nanase exists, but is no more 
than a monster of the imagination.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:37.620
She'll disappear if people 
stop fantasizing about her.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.950
Telling that truth will 
produce the same result.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:42.460
<b>Steel Lady Nanase</b>

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:42.460
In fact, there'll be more people 
writing that they hope she exists.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.100
Because that's far more interesting.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.030
But even if it is a lie,

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:53.140
New

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:53.140
New Theory

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:50.900
if we can create a story that's 
more interesting than the spectre,

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.140
people will flock to it instead.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:56.020
Though people do believe in ghosts,

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:00.400
they also wish that such 
terrifying things didn't exist.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:03.940
These desires exist on opposing 
vectors, but they coexist,

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.750
so we can easily flip their direction.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.610
I'll admit that all makes sense.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.190
Still, since you sympathize with spectres,

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:16.210
the idea of you trying to prove that 
they don't exist is basically fraud.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.920
Indeed, it is. It's all a hoax.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:23.050
But there's no other way to exterminate her.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:26.050
Let's talk about something 
a bit more realistic.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:31.460
In order to convince the forum posters 
that Steel Lady Nanase isn't a ghost,

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:33.430
we need to address two problems.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.860
First, we have to explain 
who's causing all of these

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.270
Perpetrator

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:39.770
Perpetrator

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.770
attacks around Makurazaka City.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.320
Second, we have to explain 
why they're doing it.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.570
<b>Motive</b>

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.340
If we can offer a realistic

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:49.280
and appealing solution that 
explains these two factors,

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.910
we'll be able to bind Steel Lady 
Nanase in rational fiction.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:56.970
And to make this happen, 
I need accurate information.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:01.810
If I were to write something with just 
the information that's available online

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.840
and someone points out 
later that it was in error,

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.510
our solution won't sound as credible.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:10.200
And that's exactly why I need 
more information from the police.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.100
Especially concerning Nanase Karin's death.

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:16.020
Are you asking a police officer 
to leak personal information?

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.010
What's this?

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:21.610
Nanase Haruko
Investigation Documents

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:21.610
I thought this might prove difficult since 
you're an officer in a different division,

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.570
but you already have 
documents on Nanase Karin!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.570
Nanase Haruko
Investigation Documents

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.030
Give that ba—

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:28.900
Kuro-kun!

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.710
What's with this girl?!

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:33.330
I warned you yesterday!

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.020
I told you not to get involved 
with Steel Lady Nanase!

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:38.750
But seeing how you have documents on her,

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:42.380
I'm sure you can't let 
Steel Lady Nanase go, either.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.790
As I told you yesterday,

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.320
the detective I work with 
believes Steel Lady Nanase

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.720
is part of a larger incident 
and is looking into it, so...

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.180
We have the same goal.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:52.460
We want to defeat Steel Lady Nanase,

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:54.430
and that's exactly why I need these.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.210
Will you help me out, Saki-san?

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.520
I'm fine with helping you 
gather more information,

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:03.480
but what about the perpetrator?

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:06.380
Even if you're going to make 
up some rational story,

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.950
a suspect we can actually arrest doesn't exist.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:13.020
And I don't really like the idea 
of framing someone, either.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.990
I'll figure out a way to avoid all of that.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:20.170
Our ultimate goal is to offer a story
more appealing than the truth

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:24.510
that there's some ghost 
actually causing these incidents.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.210
So it doesn't matter if we 
can't pinpoint a suspect.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:32.860
Steel Lady Nanase was deliberately 
thought up by someone.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:35.390
We just need people to believe that solution.

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:40.090
So it doesn't matter if the 
police can solve this or not.

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:42.730
As long as the people who 
believe in Steel Lady Nanase

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:47.720
are convinced by something that 
makes sense to them, we win, right?

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:48.610
Correct.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.030
That seems a bit harsh.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.580
Compared to a fake solution that relies

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:56.400
on a police investigation and trial, 
it doesn't seem that difficult.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:59.540
I guess I can at least tell you 
everything I'm allowed to tell you.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:03.170
How about we start with an outline 
and go over any questions or doubts?

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:06.910
Nanase Karin was suspected 
of killing her father,

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:10.150
and the media was after her, 
so she hid in Makurazaka City.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:14.430
Nanase Haruko

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:14.430
Her body was discovered on January 
30th of this year, just after 8:00 AM.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:17.310
One of the first questions to 
come up in the investigation

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.930
was what Nanase Karin was even doing there.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:24.100
She was found at an unattended 
construction site for a future condo.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.380
That's a very unlikely place for 
a 19-year-old girl to visit,

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:32.440
and after midnight, it was pouring, so there 
was really no one around in the area.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:36.990
It was very unnatural for her to be 
out in that weather and at that time.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.580
The only plausible explanation

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:41.620
is that someone called her 
out there to meet with her.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.250
But according to the reports, 
there were cigarettes near her body.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.340
There was an umbrella and 
five cigarette butts.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:53.220
Even in her coat pocket, they found a 
lighter and an open pack of cigarettes.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:58.290
Nanase Karin was a minor, so she 
wouldn't legally be allowed to smoke.

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:01.820
The police think that she came over here

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:05.500
to have a smoke without being noticed.

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:08.540
Nanase Karin was called out 
there to meet with someone,

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:10.920
and was smoking while waiting 
for them to show up.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:17.320
Or perhaps the person who called her 
there was already there and was smoking?

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.710
That wasn't completely ruled out.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.540
It was pouring the whole night,

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:25.210
so even if someone else was there, 
their footprints would've been washed away.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.630
But if someone was trying 
to get a hold of her,

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:30.960
you'd think there'd be a record of 
someone trying to call her phone.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.470
But all they found in her phone history

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:35.550
was her and her manager 
contacting each other.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:39.680
The police were trying to rule 
this as an accident even early on.

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.830
Steel beams suddenly falling as she was 
smoking and killing her instantly

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:46.790
would be the easiest and 
most rational explanation.

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:53.250
But if that's the case, 
some other problems arise.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:54.230
Like what?

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:56.970
The fact that there was no sign 
of her trying to defend herself

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:59.490
from the steel beams falling on her face.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.910
If a steel beam was about to fall on you, 
even if you knew it was useless,

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.170
you'd try to move away

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.580
or instinctively try to 
defend yourself somehow.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.190
But there was no sign of that,

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:13.050
so it's also questionable that 
she just let herself get crushed.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:15.010
I guess that's a good point.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.270
There was a theory that

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:19.820
if it was murder, the suspect could've hit 
her just hard enough to knock her out,

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:24.810
then laid her down on the ground, 
and just knocked the steel beams onto her.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.650
But Nanase Karin was on 
the run from the media

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:30.060
and was suspected of killing her own father.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.190
<b>Nanase Karin's True Form</b>

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.060
I'll be back soon, my dudes

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.560
They thought she might be at her wit's end.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:35.620
It seemed likely that she was desperate,

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:38.570
so if steel beams had fallen 
on her around that time,

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.320
it wouldn't be surprising if she was 
too out of it to react in time.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.570
That theory seemed more likely,

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:47.200
so the theory about someone 
knocking her out was thrown out.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:50.960
So Nanase Karin was tired 
from running from the media

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.330
and had even contemplated suicide.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.590
The steel beams fell on her amid all that,

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.590
so she just didn't bother 
to avoid getting crushed.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.720
That's another possible explanation.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:03.990
Other investigators came 
to that same conclusion.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:04.760
In the end,

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:09.890
even though the police officially 
ruled Nanase Karin's death an accident,

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.550
considering the situation, 
there was an unofficial conclusion that

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:16.150
this accidental death 
could've also been suicide.

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.380
The person who seemed most likely

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:22.660
to have a motive to kill her, her older 
sister Nanase Hatsumi, had an alibi.

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:25.590
There weren't any other likely suspects,

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:28.950
so the police came to a conclusion 
a month after her body was found.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:31.330
Her sister had a reason to kill her?

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.820
Yes. The fact that she had told others that

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:36.120
her sister was responsible 
for their father's death.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:40.540
If Nanase Karin were to die, her entire 
inheritance would go to Hatsumi.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:44.210
Basically, her younger sister dying was 
convenient to Hatsumi in many ways.

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:47.490
And among all the questions 
surrounding Nanase Karin's death,

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:50.060
Nanase Hatsumi

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:50.060
the biggest one is Nanase Hatsumi.

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:53.830
During the investigation, 
Nanase Hatsumi was the only one

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:58.320
who denied the fact that her sister 
was in a suicidal state at all.

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:04.000
It's strange that she'd object to the police's conclusion that it was an accident.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.850
You'd think an older sister 
being suspected of murder

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:08.910
would want it wrapped up quickly.

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:11.340
But it bothers me how she 
seemed convinced that if

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:13.920
her sister was going to die, 
it wouldn't be in such a way.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:17.370
So, Iwanaga, what actually happened?

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:18.380
What do you mean?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:22.180
Considering how things usually go, 
you probably know what happened.

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:24.010
I'm glad you know me so well, Senpai.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:27.390
But I didn't use my usual methods this time.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:31.130
There were too many people around during 
the day, so I couldn't go to the crime scene.

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:32.990
So why don't we head 
over there right now?

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:33.770
Go where?

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.020
We're going to go find a witness.

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:46.030
Logical Fiction

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:48.330
Why in the world did you bring me here?!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.660
It's been over six months 
since Nanase Karin died here!

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:54.370
What's the point in coming to 
the scene of the crime now?!

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.330
Correct. You won't find anything here.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.250
Which also means no one will be watching.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:02.770
And that means it's an opportune time 
for those who aren't human to act.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:09.700
All right... Let's have a look!

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.180
She's not satisfied unless 
she goes through all this.

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:18.400
It is a holy priestess's dance!

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.590
Priestesses draw magic circles now?

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:22.280
Didn't you see how cool it was?!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.310
Who are you trying to show off to?

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:27.850
Well, of course, the one 
who's about to show up.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.910
Jeez, you guys are loud.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.660
What are you doing here 
this late at night?

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:40.040
Ah, we're quite lucky to 
run into a human spirit.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.380
Oh, are you the lady 
of one eye and one leg?

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.130
All the ayakashi around town 
have been talking about you.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.270
So that would mean he's...

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:51.220
The creature that's part 
kudan and part mermaid?

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.900
He's part human, too.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:55.270
My goodness, how horrifying.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:58.610
So have you been here for a while?

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:01.150
Yup. Ever since I died last year.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:05.530
So you're aware of the accident that 
occurred here in late January, right?

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.690
An accident in which a 19-year-old girl died.

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:11.620
Oh, you mean Nanase Karin, right?

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.270
Ah, so you know of her.

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:14.540
Well, after all...

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:17.540
I witnessed the moment she died!

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:21.060
That night in the rain, she was all alone.

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:23.300
She seemed terribly depressed.

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:24.670
And then...

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:28.510
Look out!

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:40.980
She didn't even try to 
dodge the steel beams.

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:44.730
It happened so quickly! 
That was basically suicide!

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:46.990
If only I were stronger...

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:49.140
I might've been able to stop them.

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:51.820
There's no reason for 
you to feel responsible.

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:54.910
This now clarifies the truth.

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:54.910
Huh?

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.250
The Japanese police are indeed efficient.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:00.500
This is truly an accidental 
death bordering on suicide.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:03.750
W-Wait a sec! Is this really 
a good way to learn the truth?

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.750
There was no deduction 
or theorizing involved!

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:09.890
We have eyewitness account from 
an unrelated third-party witness.

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:11.090
What could be better?

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:15.510
You didn't even need to confirm 
the police investigation, then!

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:18.410
You could've found everything 
out by asking ghosts and yokai.

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:20.340
The truth is important.

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:24.320
But it's also important to see what 
is generally seen as the truth

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.110
and the conclusion that stems from it.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:30.470
That's how those on the Internet 
who fantasize about Steel Lady Nanase

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:33.070
get their ideas and function.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:36.240
Openly, I won't be using anything 
beyond what's available to them, either.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:39.160
And even if there's information 
that's not the truth

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.170
but is being believed as the 
truth, I will use that, as well.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:44.260
I am the Goddess of Wisdom.

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:47.830
If I need to make fiction sound more 
convincing to create this fiction,

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:49.760
I will use any means necessary.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:51.720
That's our lady!

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.410
I will use this frustration I'm 
feeling to do my best, as well!

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:55.900
By the time this building is done,

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:58.660
I'll be strong enough 
to be a guardian spirit!

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:04.520
All of this is starting to feel reckless.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:07.900
Even if the conclusion 
you post is well-written

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.190
and can draw people's attention,

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:12.920
in the end, whether people 
accept it or not is

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:14.830
going to depend on luck, isn't it?

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:19.510
People aren't always logical.

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:22.970
Some are impressed when 
something mystical gets resolved,

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:25.440
but others want to believe in ghosts.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:27.450
Will your lies be able to hold up

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:29.630
when we don't even know 
where that balance lies?

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:34.700
But that's also why monsters of the 
imagination aren't so easily created.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.730
We can't know if a lot 
of people will believe it

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:38.780
or not unless we give it a try.

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:41.030
Our chances against the 
rumors of Steel Lady Nanase

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:43.370
that have already spread 
aren't going to be the best.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:47.440
But every rumor is at least 
believable to some extent.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.800
Besides, we have

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.230
Kuro-senpai.

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:55.430
If there's a chance that I can 
produce a somewhat appealing lie,

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:59.330
Kuro-senpai will be able to make it 100%.

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:05.050
He didn't eat kudan meat and still 
manage to survive for nothing.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:08.250
Well, Saki-san, goodnight.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:09.800
Goodnight.

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.590
Right... Goodbye.

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:14.630
Senpai, did you get a hotel in the area?

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.010
No, I hadn't gotten that far yet.

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:21.500
I figured that might be the case, so I'm 
staying in a room with a double bed.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:24.180
I'm pretty sure I saw a 
business hotel by the station.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:27.860
Why do you refuse to sleep with me?!

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.210
Now's really not the time for that.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:30.570
Iwanaga.

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:33.690
Do you have an idea of what kind of 
"solution" you're going to create?

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:36.930
Why does the perpetrator 
take Nanase Karin's form

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.700
and attack people every night?

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:42.050
I could come up with countless motives.

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:45.780
But if you're asking whether it'll be 
impactful enough to draw attention...

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.540
It's hard to say.

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:50.110
Linking it with the past incident

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:54.540
and polishing it into more of a tearjerker 
might make it more appealing.

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:58.430
So not exactly something realistic, 
but a truth that seems more like a story.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:03.930
Yes, the world is filled with harsh truths. 
No one finds them desirable.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:07.020
It'll all be up to you 
after that, Kuro-senpai.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:10.940
Yeah, I'll go get the future that 
goes along with your solution.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:14.030
I'll die as many times 
as I need to for you.

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:18.860
There's not just a single future.

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.510
When you look into the 
future from the present,

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:25.550
it splits, changes, and spreads 
out into different paths.

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:32.580
There are paths to various kinds of 
futures, and any future is possible.

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:35.960
And when you choose a 
path and move forward,

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:40.430
all the splits behind you disappear, 
and your past becomes one path.

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:42.990
One path to the past and 
infinite paths to the future.

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:45.890
The future is always 
unknown and undecided.

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:49.190
But wouldn't that make telling 
the future impossible?

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.540
If the future continues splitting infinitely,

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:54.110
there's no way to find 
a single destination.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:57.150
But the kudan is able to predict 
the future without fail.

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:58.950
So why the contradiction?

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:01.950
The kudan doesn't make predictions 
by looking into the future.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:06.560
The kudan is able to make those 
infinite splits into a single future.

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:09.060
It has the power to determine 
which future will occur

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:11.330
and what destination awaits.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:14.290
So that's the true power 
of the prophet beast kudan?

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:17.180
<i>What a terrifying power.</i>

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:20.840
In exchange for using that power, 
the kudan loses its life.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:25.780
It looks through the endless amounts 
of futures and chooses one,

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:28.020
so its life probably burns out.

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:33.030
But it can't determine any kind of future.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:34.810
They can't use it to 
their advantage, either.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:36.480
Are there limits?

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.420
Well, if I'm not prepared to die,

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:40.780
I can't see the splits in the future and choose.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:44.820
Perhaps the kudan doesn't die 
because it states its prophecy,

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:48.380
but is able to state its prophecy 
because it's about to die.

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:53.420
Then I guess seeing the future is a 
privilege for those who are about to die.

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.310
You talk like it doesn't apply to you.

00:19:55.310 --> 00:19:57.300
Well, I can return to life.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:01.270
Also, I can only choose futures that 
have a high probability of occurring.

00:20:01.270 --> 00:20:04.440
If we're talking about 
a year into the future,

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:06.300
there are too many splits, so I can't choose.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:09.610
And if the probability of that 
future happening is too low,

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:12.440
the branch is far away 
and hard to grasp.

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:14.260
This all sounds like a pain.

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:15.470
Yeah.

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:16.850
By the way, Kuro-san,

00:20:16.850 --> 00:20:19.270
I wanted to report 
something to you today.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:20.320
Report?

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.990
Yes! I just received my 
letter of acceptance!

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.990
Iwanaga Kotoko-dono

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.990
Letter of Acceptance

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.990
We are pleased to inform you that you have passed the entrance exam
for our law program.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.030
Oh, congrats.

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:29.240
We'll be going to the same university 
in the spring, Kuro-senpai.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:33.270
Kuro-senpai, when Steel Lady 
Nanase killed you earlier,

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:36.170
were you not able to see a 
future in which she was destroyed?

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:39.330
There probably was one,
but I couldn't reach it.

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:42.900
There were too many splits, so I 
couldn't sort through them in time.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:45.800
Determining the best future 
to defeat that thing

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:48.220
and coming back to life 
took everything out of me.

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:50.280
Though, you didn't actually defeat her.

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:53.100
You always think you can 
solve everything on your own.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.020
Look who's talking.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:58.400
I can come back to life, 
but if you die, that's it.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:02.690
<i>You leave me alone for a week, and now you 
act like you're my guardian or something?</i>

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:08.930
<i>Back then, Senpai died once, 
determined a future, and came back.</i>

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:12.630
<i>But even then, he couldn't choose 
a future where he was able to</i>

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:15.120
<i>defeat Steel Lady Nanase and win.</i>

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:18.880
<i>That was a future outside 
of Senpai's grasp.</i>

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:22.300
<i>That's why I have to make 
it something obtainable.</i>

00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:26.610
<i>If I can at least set up an opportunity, 
we can defeat Steel Lady Nanase.</i>

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:30.540
<i>Senpai will make that opportunity a reality.</i>

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:34.550
So you haven't told Saki-san 
about <i>her</i>, have you?

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:37.520
Not a single word.

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:42.450
Yeah. It hasn't been determined that 
she's actually involved in any of this.

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:45.570
Senpai, didn't you try 
picking a future where you

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.790
and Saki-san didn't break up 
with your power over the future?

00:21:48.790 --> 00:21:50.030
If I can do that,

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:53.760
I'm going to go grab a future where 
it's okay for me to break up with you.

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:56.660
Th-That's totally unfair! 
How dastardly can you get?!

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:58.830
Stop laughing!

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:00.750
<b>Makurazaka Central Park</b>

00:21:59.470 --> 00:22:00.750
Don't worry.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.590
It's not as if I think I can 
get back with Saki-san.

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:05.510
I'm pretty sure she feels the same way.

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:08.980
I don't appreciate you two 
agreeing like that, either.

00:22:08.980 --> 00:22:11.140
So what exactly do you want me to say?

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:14.350
Passionately say that you'll 
make me happy, no matter what.

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:16.770
What's so funny?

00:22:17.610 --> 00:22:21.400
<i>Kuro-senpai's attachments to 
others can seem rather weak.</i>

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:25.500
<i>So weak that I can see him leaving 
me one day and seeing it as a favor.</i>

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:29.520
<i>He's such a pain.</i>

00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:33.160
<i>Why can't you be true to your feelings?</i>

00:22:33.730 --> 00:22:36.660
Let's head to the hotel. Once you 
get through the park, turn right.

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:37.910
Okay.

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:40.540
<i>I need to think.</i>

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:45.460
<i>If a victim turns up, creating this 
solution will become even more difficult.</i>

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:49.590
<i>It's okay. I'm sure Steel Lady Nanase 
won't be able to kill anyone yet.</i>

00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:55.370
<i>As long as no one tries to approach 
her, nothing should happen tonight.</i>

00:22:56.070 --> 00:22:57.270
I'm a police officer.

00:22:57.270 --> 00:23:00.270
What are you doing at this 
hour dressed like that?

00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:02.610
<i>Just like the rumors said...</i>

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:06.360
<i>A woman without a face, wearing a 
red dress, and carrying a steel beam.</i>

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:09.340
<i>Are they using special effects 
makeup? It's pretty well-done.</i>

00:23:09.340 --> 00:23:11.610
<i>Is she charging me? 
Then I have no choice.</i>

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:17.410
<i>What...</i>

00:23:18.010 --> 00:23:19.430
<i>What just happened?</i>

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:26.900
